Inside __invoke<_Transform, void (*)(), int>, instantiated from
_Binder::_S_call, decltype(_S_test<_Callable, _Args...>(0)) is the type of
the variadic C-style operator() (_Partial): the constrained
two-parameter template is not selected.  With the template arguments
spelled out, and in main, it is.  Reduced from
cpp20_range_adaptor_closure_invoked_through_invoke_impl (cvise, oracle:
both forms in the same run, the compilers accepting both as
static_asserts).
